KG42.register("clusters-30e54361bd92fcdd93d00aff",{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v142-d-K005","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","label":"Fixed tariffs and residual-power bidding in islanded emergency energy supply","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K005","label":"Fixed tariffs and residual-power bidding in islanded emergency energy supply","market_meaning":"When the physical microgrid disconnects from the grid and enters islanded operation, critical facilities receive energy under a fixed-tariff arrangement, and residential and commercial users bear a bidding obligation for the residual power. The two chains jointly express the differentiated energy supply arrangements under the same emergency scenario, but have not yet formed complete allocation, pricing, and supply-demand balance rules.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M02"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"compatible","scope_explanation":"The two chains come from the same physical islanded operation passage, and their applicable conditions are compatible with the participant classification. This scenario belongs to M02; the double auction, uniform clearing price, or trial fixed price of the M01 virtual market is not moved into this cluster; the stage union includes only bidding and pricing in the supplied chains.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The critical-facility arrangement and residual-power bidding share explicit emergency conditions and a resource allocation context and are complementary beneficiary-category arrangements. Only their procedural connection is retained; no clearing edge, precise priority algorithm, or continuous energy supply guarantee is added from paragraph order.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R013","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Retain the bidding obligation of residential and commercial users for residual power under islanded conditions."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R014","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Retain the fixed-rate energy supply arrangement for critical facilities under the same islanded condition."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K005-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R014","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R013","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e25"],"rationale":"The same paragraph separately specifies the fixed rate for critical facilities and the bidding for surplus electricity by residential and commercial users; the two chains complement the category division of labor within the same emergency energy supply arrangement; this connection does not define the formula for surplus electricity or the bidding clearing method."}],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K005-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"No fixed-rate value, unit, or setting method is given, nor are the energy supply quantity for critical facilities, the definition of surplus electricity, the bid format, the bid allocation, or the winning-bid payment rules given. The order and price mathematics of M01 cannot be directly adopted to fill in these contents.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R013","v141-c-R014"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C001","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e25"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Re-extract the fixed rate and the definition of surplus electricity bidding according to the M02 scope; implement the existing C2 revision request for R014, and where the source does not provide it, continue to maintain a procedural formulation."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K005-G02","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The dedicated proposals for islanding activation status, critical facility categories, and the fixed-rate arrangement have not been approved. R014 continues to use pricing.local, but that node is defined in the framework as a clearing price and is not fully consistent with the current fixed arrangement; the same node name must not be treated as being the same as the M01 price.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R013","v141-c-R014"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R013::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R014::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C001","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e25","v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g03-e003","v141-b-g03-e004"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g02-prop-island-mode","v141-b-g02-prop-critical-facility-fixed-rate","v141-b-g03-p02","v141-b-g03-p03"],"required_work":"Manually review the activation and beneficiary category proposals and their overlap, check the rate interpretation of fixed rates and node adaptation, and then have C supplement the approved representation; no new node is inserted this time."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K005-G03","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The M02 source also states that within the island, balance must be maintained by relying on existing generation, that the physical scope does not cover the entire virtual market, and that there are long-term reliable energy supply and energy storage gaps; the current two chains do not express these operational constraints, and the fixed arrangement cannot be interpreted as an unconditional guarantee of continuous energy supply.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R013","v141-c-R014"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C001","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g02-e27","v141-b-g03-e004"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should retrieve, within M02, the content on physical coverage, activation, supply-demand balance, and capability limits; establish the corresponding chain only when the source supports it, and do not derive physical energy supply closure from virtual trading rules."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K005-G04","category":"unverified_source","description":"The evidence for the islanded arrangement and operational capability remains unverified; the complementary relationship in the same paragraph supports only the current candidate assembly and does not indicate that the rate interpretation or the emergency allocation mechanism has been reviewed and confirmed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R013","v141-c-R014"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e25","v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g02-e27","v141-b-g03-e003","v141-b-g03-e004"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually verify the physical islanded conditions, the fixed arrangement, and the wording on surplus electricity, while keeping the M02 and M01 scopes separate."}]},"rule_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R013","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R014"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-3fdc8e6f56f1ec47","COMP-f3589aa8b8a36e3e"]});
